concepts.body:
```bash
npx librocat start            # http://127.0.0.1:4747/mcp, over ./okf
LIBROCAT_BUNDLE=~/notes/okf npx librocat start --port 4800
```

`start` serves Streamable HTTP on loopback only, so any number of agents on
this machine share one library. Point each at the URL, for example
`claude mcp add --transport http librocat-local http://127.0.0.1:4747/mcp`,
or `{ "url": "http://127.0.0.1:4747/mcp" }` in any MCP config.

An agent that spawns its servers over stdio instead runs the same library
itself:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "librocat": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "librocat", "mcp"],
      "env": { "LIBROCAT_BUNDLE": "./okf" }
    }
  }
}
```

The Agent Skills are the same for a local and a hosted library:
`npx skills add librocat/librocat`.

The dashboard is built from shadcn/ui throughout:
  - the sidebar layout, with a user menu and breadcrumbs;
  - Field forms, and an eight-digit code input for sign-in codes;
  - Empty states, Skeleton loading screens, and a Switch for
    pay-as-you-go;
  - tooltips on copy buttons.
